            <ArticleTitle>Testicular torsion in spinal cord injury: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>163-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/sc.2015.11</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Case report.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe a case of testicular torsion in spinal cord injury (SCI).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">Physical Medicine Rehabilitation Training and Research Hospital in Turkey.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We present the first case of testicular torsion in SCI along with its clinical presentation and follow-up results.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Testicular torsion is a rare condition. No case was reported in people with SCI so far. The main difficulty in the diagnosis is that the nociceptive pain is below the injury level and the acute condition could be overlooked.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Testicular torsion is an acute condition for which early diagnosis is critical in the treatment. The case we describe adds new pitfalls in the diagnosis of this rare condition in people with SCI from the perspective of nociceptive pain below the injury level.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
